    {"id":"sec-kernel-4","title":"Purity and proof","level":2,"document":"doc-kernel","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:krn-012}}\n\n{{entity:krn-013}}\n\n{{entity:krn-014}}\n\n{{entity:krn-015}}\n\n{{entity:krn-016}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-storage-1","title":"Storage","level":1,"document":"doc-storage","order":1,"body":"\nThe store contract is the only way to a tenant database. An adapter is accepted by passing the conformance table, whatever database is behind it.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-storage-2","title":"Adapters","level":2,"document":"doc-storage","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:sto-001}}\n\n{{entity:sto-002}}\n\n{{entity:sto-003}}\n\n{{entity:sto-004}}\n\n{{entity:sto-005}}\n\n{{entity:sto-006}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-runtime-1","title":"Runtime, gateway and simulator","level":1,"document":"doc-runtime","order":1,"body":"\nThese statements describe behaviour the prototype already has. Each is tied to a test that exists, so the first milestone starts with a recorded passing run.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-runtime-2","title":"Runtime","level":2,"document":"doc-runtime","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:run-001}}\n\n{{entity:run-002}}\n\n{{entity:run-003}}\n\n{{entity:run-004}}\n\n{{entity:run-005}}\n\n"},
