    {"id":"sec-workflows-251","title":"Reach","level":2,"document":"doc-workflows","order":251,"body":"\n{{entity:wfl-256}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-threat-250","title":"Threat model","level":1,"document":"doc-threat","order":250,"body":"\nThe attack classes that cut across components, and the requirement that refuses each one at the boundary where it arrives. A requirement that names a component states the refusal that component makes.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-threat-251","title":"Responses and transport","level":2,"document":"doc-threat","order":251,"body":"\n{{entity:thr-250}}\n\n{{entity:thr-251}}\n\n{{entity:thr-252}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-threat-252","title":"Reachability","level":2,"document":"doc-threat","order":252,"body":"\n{{entity:thr-253}}\n\n{{entity:thr-254}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-threat-253","title":"Supply chain","level":2,"document":"doc-threat","order":253,"body":"\n{{entity:thr-255}}\n\n{{entity:thr-256}}\n\n{{entity:thr-257}}\n\n{{entity:thr-258}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-threat-254","title":"Incidents and disclosure","level":2,"document":"doc-threat","order":254,"body":"\n{{entity:thr-259}}\n\n{{entity:thr-260}}\n\n{{entity:thr-261}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-threat-255","title":"Abuse and takedown","level":2,"document":"doc-threat","order":255,"body":"\n{{entity:thr-262}}\n\n{{entity:thr-263}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-index-1","title":"Specification","level":1,"document":"doc-index","order":1,"body":"\nRequirements derived from [the white paper](00-vision/whitepaper.md), in the format Concordance lints. Each one names the boundary it is observed at, what it traces to, how it is proved and the milestone at which it is first verified. Case tables live beside their file, in `cases/`.\n\n| File | Prefix | Covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| [01-core/kernel.md](01-core/kernel.md) | KRN | The pure transition function, its invariants and the abstract model |\n| [01-core/storage.md](01-core/storage.md) | STO | The store contract and its adapters |\n| [01-core/runtime.md](01-core/runtime.md) | RUN, GWY, SIM | What the existing services and the simulator guarantee today |\n| [02-tenancy/tenancy.md](02-tenancy/tenancy.md) | TEN | The control plane, the tenant directory and the life of a tenant |\n| [03-identity/identity.md](03-identity/identity.md) | IDN | Realms, sign-in methods, sessions, factors and recovery |\n| [03-identity/federation.md](03-identity/federation.md) | FED | OpenID Connect, SAML and SCIM |\n| [03-identity/tokens.md](03-identity/tokens.md) | TOK | Service accounts, agent identities, delegation and signing keys |\n| [04-automation/scheduling.md](04-automation/scheduling.md) | SCH | Jobs, schedules, triggers and leases |\n| [04-automation/workflows.md](04-automation/workflows.md) | WFL | Workflows as metadata, connectors and scheduled publication |\n| [05-delivery/copies.md](05-delivery/copies.md) | CPY | How data is kept outside its owner for cheaper reads, and how it stays right |\n| [05-delivery/edge.md](05-delivery/edge.md) | EDG | The content delivery network, domains, certificates and limits |\n| [06-agents/operations.md](06-agents/operations.md) | AGT | The operation catalogue, dry runs, proposals and limits on agents |\n| [06-agents/observability.md](06-agents/observability.md) | OBS | Telemetry, correlation, health and the audit log |\n| [07-content/content.md](07-content/content.md) | CMS | Content types, versions, media, languages and preview |\n| [08-platform/platform.md](08-platform/platform.md) | DEP, SEC, ASR | The local stack, the cloud profile, keys and the assurance loop |\n| [09-threat/threat-model.md](09-threat/threat-model.md) | THR | The attack classes that cut across components: response headers, transport, reachability, supply chain, incidents and abuse |\n\n"}
  ],
  "caseTables": [
    {"id":"cases-storage-conformance","path":"specifications/01-core/cases/storage-conformance.md","title":"Storage conformance","document":"doc-cases-storage-conformance","body":"# Storage conformance\n\nEvery check an adapter of the store contract passes. The checks are run by `strata_storage_api::conformance::run` against a fresh, empty store.\n\n## Cases\n\n| Case | Establishes |\n|---|---|\n| absent-tenant | A tenant that does not exist loads as absent, with no events |\n| state-equals-kernel | After a sequence of intents the stored state has the canonical hash of the state the kernel computed |\n| stale-commit | A commit based on an old revision conflicts and changes nothing |\n| malformed-commit | A commit whose events do not continue the sequence is refused whole |\n| partial-load | A load returns the records its needs name, and the tenant header |\n| list-containment | A lookup by value finds records whose list field contains the value |\n| tenant-isolation | Equal record identifiers in two tenants resolve to different records |\n| outbox-order | Unpublished events are returned in commit order across tenants until marked published |\n| journal-replay | The journal replays through the kernel to the stored state |\n| sessions | Sessions are stored, found by token hash, revoked with a commit and purged |\n| accounts | A login is scoped to its tenant |\n| snapshots | A snapshot restores to a state with the same canonical hash |\n| reset | A reset removes everything |\n","columns":["Case","Establishes"],"rowCount":13},
    {"id":"cases-sign-in-methods","path":"specifications/03-identity/cases/sign-in-methods.md","title":"Sign-in methods","document":"doc-cases-sign-in-methods","body":"# Sign-in methods\n\nEach row is one presentation of one method and whether it yields a session.\n\n## Cases\n\n| Case | Method | Presented | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| password-correct | password | the stored password | accepted |\n| password-wrong | password | another password | refused |\n| password-unknown-account | password | a name with no account | refused, in the time a wrong password takes |\n| password-domain-bound | password | a correct password for an address in a provider-bound domain | refused |\n| passkey-valid | passkey | an assertion for the tenant address signed by a registered credential | accepted |\n| passkey-other-origin | passkey | an assertion made for another address | refused |\n| passkey-counter-regress | passkey | an assertion whose signature counter went backwards | refused |\n| link-first-use | emailed link | a fresh link in the requesting browser | accepted |\n| link-second-use | emailed link | a link already used | refused |\n| link-expired | emailed link | a link past its lifetime | refused |\n| link-other-browser | emailed link | a fresh link in another browser | refused |\n| oidc-valid | OpenID Connect | a callback with the pending state and a token that verifies | accepted |\n| oidc-wrong-state | OpenID Connect | a callback with a state that matches no pending request | refused |\n| oidc-wrong-audience | OpenID Connect | a token issued to another client | refused |\n| oidc-wrong-nonce | OpenID Connect | a token whose nonce differs from the pending request | refused |\n| saml-valid | SAML | a response to a pending request signed by a configured certificate | accepted |\n| saml-unsigned | SAML | a response with no signature on its assertion | refused |\n| saml-replayed | SAML | an assertion presented a second time | refused |\n| saml-unsolicited | SAML | a response to no pending request, provider-started sign-in off | refused |\n| second-factor-missing | any | a first factor alone under a policy asking for two | no session until the second factor verifies |\n","columns":["Case","Method","Presented","Outcome"],"rowCount":20},
    {"id":"cases-provisioning-operations","path":"specifications/03-identity/cases/provisioning-operations.md","title":"Provisioning operations","document":"doc-cases-provisioning-operations","body":"# Provisioning operations\n\nThe SCIM 2.0 operations the provisioning endpoint supports and their effect on the realm.\n\n## Cases\n\n| Case | Operation | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| create-user | POST /Users | a principal exists with the external identifier linked |\n| create-duplicate | POST /Users with a user name in use | refused with a uniqueness error |\n| replace-user | PUT /Users/{id} | the attributes of the principal are replaced |\n| patch-deactivate | PATCH /Users/{id} active false | the principal is disabled and its sessions are revoked |\n| patch-reactivate | PATCH /Users/{id} active true | the principal can sign in again |\n| delete-user | DELETE /Users/{id} | the principal is removed and its sessions are revoked |\n| filter-user-name | GET /Users?filter=userName eq | the matching principal, or an empty list |\n| group-membership | PATCH /Groups/{id} members | the roles mapped from the group are granted or removed |\n| wrong-tenant-token | a request with a token of another tenant | refused |\n","columns":["Case","Operation","Effect"],"rowCount":9},
    {"id":"cases-copy-classes","path":"specifications/05-delivery/cases/copy-classes.md","title":"Copy classes","document":"doc-cases-copy-classes","body":"# Copy classes\n\nEvery class of stored copy. The data model of this specification declares the same classes as copies, and Exegra checks them against its data rules.\n\n## Cases\n\n| Case | Holds | Held by | Scope | Key | Freshness bound | Erasure point |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| compiled-schema | the schema of a tenant and its compiled expressions | runtime, in process | kept by the server | tenant, schema version | none: a new version is a new key | dropped when the tenant is deleted or the process ends |\n| directory-entry | tenant state, placement and domain bindings | gateway and runtime, in process | kept by the server | host name or tenant | 30 seconds | the next refresh after a tenant is deleted |\n| session-assertion | the principal and roles of one session | gateway, in process | per session | hash of the session secret | 5 seconds | the revocation notice, or the next recheck |\n| public-view | the published fields of the records a view shows | copy store | shared | tenant, view, arguments, schema version, revisions | none: a new revision is a new key | superseded by the commit of the deletion |\n| audience-view | the fields of a view as one audience class may read them | copy store | per principal class | tenant, view, arguments, audience class, schema version, revisions | none: a new revision is a new key | superseded by the commit of the deletion |\n| edge-page | a rendered public page | content delivery network | shared | host name, path | 5 seconds after a purge, and the lifetime as backstop | the purge sent by the commit of the deletion |\n| edge-asset | a static asset | content delivery network | shared | host name, address derived from content | none: content decides the address | not applicable: holds no tenant record |\n| edge-media | a media rendition | content delivery network | shared, or per principal through a signed address | host name, content hash | none: content decides the address | the purge sent when the file is deleted |\n","columns":["Case","Holds","Held by","Scope","Key","Freshness bound","Erasure point"],"rowCount":8},
    {"id":"cases-seams","path":"specifications/08-platform/cases/seams.md","title":"Seams","document":"doc-cases-seams","body":"# Seams\n\nEvery dependency on infrastructure, the contract that hides it, and the adapters behind the contract.\n\n## Cases\n\n| Case | Contract | Local adapter | Cloud adapter |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| store | B-2 store contract | PostgreSQL in a container, SQLite for one process | managed PostgreSQL |\n| files | B-14 file store contract | an S3-compatible object store in a container | object storage |\n| copies | B-15 copy store contract | a key-value store in a container | managed key-value store |\n| wake | B-16 wake contract | PostgreSQL notifications | a managed queue |\n| keys | B-17 key service contract | a key file on a local volume | the provider key service |\n| mail | B-18 mail contract | a mail catcher in a container | the provider mail service |\n| edge | B-10 edge contract | a caching reverse proxy in a container | the content delivery network |\n| identity-providers | B-5 federation endpoints | a test identity provider in a container | the tenant's providers |\n| telemetry | B-12 telemetry export | a collector in a container | a collector exporting to the provider |\n| limits | B-100 limit contract | a key-value store in a container | managed key-value store |\n| backup | B-101 backup archive contract | an S3-compatible object store in a container, with point-in-time archives of each database | object storage with point-in-time recovery |\n","columns":["Case","Contract","Local adapter","Cloud adapter"],"rowCount":11},
    {"id":"cases-seams","path":"specifications/08-platform/cases/seams.md","title":"Seams","document":"doc-cases-seams","body":"# Seams\n\nEvery dependency on infrastructure, the contract that hides it, and the adapters behind the contract.\n\n## Cases\n\n| Case | Contract | Local adapter | Cloud adapter |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| store | B-2 store contract | PostgreSQL in a container, SQLite for one process | managed PostgreSQL |\n| files | B-14 file store contract | an S3-compatible object store in a container | object storage |\n| copies | B-15 copy store contract | a key-value store in a container | managed key-value store |\n| wake | B-16 wake contract | PostgreSQL notifications | a managed queue |\n| keys | B-17 key service contract | a key file on a local volume | the provider key service |\n| mail | B-18 mail contract | a mail catcher in a container | the provider mail service |\n| edge | B-10 edge contract | a caching reverse proxy in a container | the content delivery network |\n| identity-providers | B-5 federation endpoints | a test identity provider in a container | the tenant's providers |\n| telemetry | B-12 telemetry export | a collector in a container | a collector exporting to the provider |\n| search | B-151 search index contract | PostgreSQL full-text search in the tenant database | managed search service |\n","columns":["Case","Contract","Local adapter","Cloud adapter"],"rowCount":10},
    {"id":"cases-budget-measurement","path":"specifications/08-platform/cases/budget-measurement.md","title":"Budget measurement","document":"doc-cases-budget-measurement","body":"# Budget measurement\n\nHow each budget is measured. A budget is verified by a recorded measurement taken as its row describes.\n\n## Cases\n\n| Case | Requirement | Measure | Bound | Measured on |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| provision-time | TEN-004 | time from the provisioning request to the directory reporting active | 30 seconds, 95th percentile | the local stack, 100 tenants in sequence |\n| revocation-reach | IDN-014 | time from revocation to refusal at each gateway instance | 5 seconds, worst case | the local stack with three gateway instances and the notice dropped |\n| session-lookup | IDN-015 | response time of a session lookup | 20 ms, 99th percentile | the local stack under the reference load |\n| token-lifetime | TOK-005 | expiry minus issue time of issued tokens | 10 minutes, maximum | every token issued in the test run |\n| job-start | SCH-002 | start time minus due time | 5 seconds, 99th percentile | the local stack, 1000 tenants with one due job each |\n| change-visible | CPY-009 | time from commit to the delivery interface answering with the change | 2 seconds, 99th percentile | the local stack under the reference load |\n| copy-hit-share | CPY-010 | share of delivery requests answered without a tenant database query | 95 percent, minimum | the local stack under the reference read load |\n| purge-reach | EDG-007 | time from commit to the edge answering with the change | 5 seconds, 99th percentile | the cloud profile |\n| zone-loss | DEP-010 | time from loss of a zone to requests being served | 15 minutes | a drill in the cloud profile |\n| restore-loss | DEP-011 | age of the newest change missing after a restore | 5 minutes, maximum | a drill in the cloud profile |\n","columns":["Case","Requirement","Measure","Bound","Measured on"],"rowCount":10}
    {"id":"cases-seams","path":"specifications/08-platform/cases/seams.md","title":"Seams","document":"doc-cases-seams","body":"# Seams\n\nEvery dependency on infrastructure, the contract that hides it, and the adapters behind the contract.\n\n## Cases\n\n| Case | Contract | Local adapter | Cloud adapter |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| store | B-2 store contract | PostgreSQL in a container, SQLite for one process | managed PostgreSQL |\n| files | B-14 file store contract | an S3-compatible object store in a container | object storage |\n| copies | B-15 copy store contract | a key-value store in a container | managed key-value store |\n| wake | B-16 wake contract | PostgreSQL notifications | a managed queue |\n| keys | B-17 key service contract | a key file on a local volume | the provider key service |\n| mail | B-18 mail contract | a mail catcher in a container | the provider mail service |\n| edge | B-10 edge contract | a caching reverse proxy in a container | the content delivery network |\n| identity-providers | B-5 federation endpoints | a test identity provider in a container | the tenant's providers |\n| telemetry | B-12 telemetry export | a collector in a container | a collector exporting to the provider |\n| model | B-201 model provider contract | a local model adapter in a container, replying from fixed scripts | a hosted model service of the tenant's chosen provider |\n","columns":["Case","Contract","Local adapter","Cloud adapter"],"rowCount":10},
    {"id":"cases-model-provider-conformance","path":"specifications/09-conversation/cases/model-provider-conformance.md","title":"Model provider conformance","document":"doc-cases-model-provider-conformance","body":"# Model provider conformance\n\nEvery check an adapter of the model provider contract passes. The checks run against the local model adapter and against each hosted adapter.\n\n## Cases\n\n| Case | Establishes |\n|---|---|\n| reply-streams | A reply arrives as parts in order and ends in one recorded state |\n| cancel-stops | A cancelled reply stops producing output |\n| tool-request-named | A tool request names an operation from the catalogue it was given |\n| markup-kept-as-text | Markup in a reply reaches the conversation as text |\n| usage-reported | Token counts are reported for each reply |\n| unnamed-provider-refused | A request to a provider that the tenant policy does not name is refused before any content is sent |\n| fixed-replay | The local adapter returns the same reply for the same request |\n","columns":["Case","Establishes"],"rowCount":7},
    {"id":"cases-budget-measurement","path":"specifications/08-platform/cases/budget-measurement.md","title":"Budget measurement","document":"doc-cases-budget-measurement","body":"# Budget measurement\n\nHow each budget is measured. A budget is verified by a recorded measurement taken as its row describes.\n\n## Cases\n\n| Case | Requirement | Measure | Bound | Measured on |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| provision-time | TEN-004 | time from the provisioning request to the directory reporting active | 30 seconds, 95th percentile | the local stack, 100 tenants in sequence |\n| revocation-reach | IDN-014 | time from revocation to refusal at each gateway instance | 5 seconds, worst case | the local stack with three gateway instances and the notice dropped |\n| session-lookup | IDN-015 | response time of a session lookup | 20 ms, 99th percentile | the local stack under the reference load |\n| token-lifetime | TOK-005 | expiry minus issue time of issued tokens | 10 minutes, maximum | every token issued in the test run |\n| job-start | SCH-002 | start time minus due time | 5 seconds, 99th percentile | the local stack, 1000 tenants with one due job each |\n| change-visible | CPY-009 | time from commit to the delivery interface answering with the change | 2 seconds, 99th percentile | the local stack under the reference load |\n| copy-hit-share | CPY-010 | share of delivery requests answered without a tenant database query | 95 percent, minimum | the local stack under the reference read load |\n| purge-reach | EDG-007 | time from commit to the edge answering with the change | 5 seconds, 99th percentile | the cloud profile |\n| zone-loss | DEP-010 | time from loss of a zone to requests being served | 15 minutes | a drill in the cloud profile |\n| restore-loss | DEP-011 | age of the newest change missing after a restore | 5 minutes, maximum | a drill in the cloud profile |\n| first-part | CNV-224 | time from acceptance of the person's message to the first part of the reply | 1 second, 95th percentile | the local stack with the model adapter replying from a fixed script, 200 turns in sequence |\n| cancel-effect | CNV-225 | time from the cancellation to the stop of model output and of uncommitted operations | 1 second, 99th percentile | the local stack, 500 cancellations under the reference load |\n| preview-time | CNV-211 | time from the change request to the preview being answered | 3 seconds, 95th percentile | the local stack, a tenant of one hundred thousand records |\n| announcement-rate | CNV-240 | interval between two announcements of the live region during one streamed reply | 10 seconds, minimum interval | the accessibility harness reading the live region of a 1000-part reply |\n| stream-resume | CNV-242 | time from restoration of a dropped connection to the next part of the stream | 3 seconds, 95th percentile | the local stack behind a proxy that drops connections, 100 drops |\n| touch-target | CNV-243 | smallest size of a control of the conversation, in each direction | 24 CSS pixels, minimum | automated layout check at a width of 360 CSS pixels |\n| reply-reflow | CNV-244 | horizontal scroll width of a reply | 0 CSS pixels beyond a width of 360 CSS pixels | automated layout check at a width of 360 CSS pixels |\n| autosave-delay | UXA-204 | time from the last edit to the saved draft | 2 seconds, 95th percentile | the local stack, 100 edits in sequence |\n| presence-delay | UXA-208 | time from another editor's change of presence to its display | 3 seconds, 95th percentile | the local stack with two editors on one record |\n| signin-first-content | UXA-213 | time from the request of the sign-in page to its first content | 1 second, 95th percentile | the local stack behind a connection of 1.6 megabits per second and 150 ms round trip |\n| authoring-reflow | UXA-214 | horizontal scroll width of each view | 0 CSS pixels beyond a width of 360 CSS pixels | automated layout check of each view at 360 CSS pixels |\n","columns":["Case","Requirement","Measure","Bound","Measured on"],"rowCount":21}
  ],

  // ---- Views -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  "views": [
    {"id":"architecture","name":"Architecture","projection":"structural","description":"Every component and the relationships between them."},
    {"id":"trust-zones","name":"Trust zones","projection":"structural","description":"The same components, coloured by trust zone.","display":{"colorBy":"trustZone"}},
    {"id":"data","name":"Data","projection":"data","description":"Records, the copies made of them, and who holds each."},
    {"id":"traceability","name":"Traceability","projection":"references","description":"Goals, constraints, decisions, boundaries and requirements, and the references between them.","display":{"depth":1}},
    {"id":"requirements","name":"Requirements and claims","projection":"claims","description":"Every requirement and every model claim, by status."},
    {"id":"behaviour","name":"Behaviour","projection":"behavior","description":"The behaviour models and their scenarios."}
  ],

  // ---- Behaviour models: assumptions, events, behaviours, faults, scenarios ----------------------
  "assumptions": [
    {"id":"a-planning-rates","statement":"The failure rates in the fault model are planning estimates, not measurements.","rationale":"No deployment exists yet. They are replaced by measured rates when one does."},
    {"id":"a-provider-signatures","statement":"A signature that verifies against a key published by an identity provider was made by that provider.","rationale":"Federation rests on the provider keeping its signing keys."},
    {"id":"a-mailbox-control","statement":"Only the owner of an address reads mail sent to it.","rationale":"An emailed link is as strong as the mailbox it is sent to. Binding the link to the requesting browser narrows this."},
    {"id":"a-database-commit","statement":"The tenant database confirms a commit only when the transaction is durable, and checks a fencing token atomically with the write.","rationale":"The lease and outbox models depend on it. The conformance suite checks it for each adapter."},
    {"id":"a-clock-skew","statement":"The clocks of platform components differ by less than half a second.","rationale":"Lifetimes and bounds are compared across components."},
    {"id":"a-model-abstraction","statement":"The behaviour models are abstractions of code that is not written yet, and say what that code is to do.","rationale":"Until an implementation exists, a verified model claim is a statement about the design."}
  ],
  "events": [
    {"id":"ml-requested","name":"Link requested","description":"A person asks for a sign-in link."},
    {"id":"ml-mailed","name":"Link mailed","description":"The identity service sends the link."},
    {"id":"ml-presented","name":"Link presented","description":"A browser presents a link.","payload":[{"name":"token","type":"string"},{"name":"browser","type":"string"}]},
    {"id":"ml-session-issued","name":"Session issued from a link","description":"The link was accepted."},
    {"id":"ml-refused","name":"Link refused","description":"The link was not accepted."},
    {"id":"oidc-started","name":"OpenID Connect sign-in started","description":"A person chooses a provider."},
    {"id":"oidc-redirected","name":"Redirected to the provider","description":"The browser is sent to the provider with a state value."},
    {"id":"oidc-callback","name":"Callback received","description":"A callback arrives.","payload":[{"name":"state","type":"string"}]},
    {"id":"oidc-session-issued","name":"Session issued from a provider","description":"The callback was accepted and the token verified."},
    {"id":"oidc-refused","name":"Callback refused","description":"The callback was not accepted."},
    {"id":"sr-revoked","name":"Session revoked","description":"A session is revoked."},
    {"id":"sr-notice","name":"Revocation notice","description":"The identity service tells gateways about a revocation."},
    {"id":"sr-request","name":"Request with the session","description":"A request arrives at the gateway carrying the session."},
    {"id":"sr-lookup","name":"Session lookup","description":"The gateway asks the identity service about the session."},
    {"id":"sr-lookup-answer","name":"Session lookup answer","description":"The identity service answers.","payload":[{"name":"valid","type":"boolean"}]},
    {"id":"sr-accepted","name":"Request accepted","description":"The gateway treated the session as valid."},
    {"id":"sr-refused","name":"Request refused","description":"The gateway refused the session."},
    {"id":"job-due","name":"Job due","description":"A job reaches its due time."},
    {"id":"lease-granted","name":"Lease granted","description":"A worker is given the job under a new token."},
    {"id":"lease-expired","name":"Lease expired","description":"The lease ran out with no result."},
    {"id":"work-reported","name":"Work reported","description":"A worker reports a result with the token it holds.","payload":[{"name":"token","type":"number"}]},
    {"id":"job-completed","name":"Job completed","description":"The result was recorded."},
    {"id":"result-refused","name":"Result refused","description":"The result was not recorded."},
    {"id":"ec-published","name":"Content published","description":"A change to a published record commits."},
    {"id":"ec-purge","name":"Purge","description":"The surrogate keys of the changed record are purged."},
    {"id":"ec-request","name":"Reader request","description":"A reader asks the edge for the page."},
    {"id":"ec-origin-fetch","name":"Origin fetch","description":"The edge asks the origin."},
    {"id":"ec-origin-answer","name":"Origin answer","description":"The origin answers with the current version.","payload":[{"name":"version","type":"number"}]},
    {"id":"ec-served","name":"Page served","description":"The edge answers the reader."},
    {"id":"pv-requested","name":"Tenant requested","description":"A tenant is to be provisioned."},
    {"id":"pv-database-created","name":"Database created","description":"The tenant database exists."},
    {"id":"pv-layout-applied","name":"Layout applied","description":"The storage layout is in place."},
    {"id":"pv-template-installed","name":"Template installed","description":"The template was installed through kernel intents."},
    {"id":"pv-activated","name":"Tenant activated","description":"The directory reports the tenant as active."},
    {"id":"pv-step-failed","name":"Provisioning step failed","description":"A step of provisioning failed."},
    {"id":"pv-rolled-back","name":"Provisioning rolled back","description":"What was created has been removed."},
    {"id":"cp-proposed","name":"Change proposed","description":"A change is submitted.","payload":[{"name":"risky","type":"boolean"}]},
    {"id":"cp-projected","name":"Change projected","description":"The projection of the change has run."},
    {"id":"cp-approved","name":"Proposal approved","description":"A permitted principal approved."},
    {"id":"cp-rejected","name":"Proposal rejected","description":"A permitted principal rejected."},
    {"id":"cp-apply-requested","name":"Apply requested","description":"Someone asks for the change to be applied."},
    {"id":"cp-applied","name":"Change applied","description":"The change was committed."},
    {"id":"cp-refused","name":"Apply refused","description":"The change was not committed."},
    {"id":"rt-intent","name":"Intent received","description":"The runtime receives an intent."},
    {"id":"rt-decided","name":"Transition decided","description":"The kernel accepted the intent."},
    {"id":"rt-committed","name":"Commit confirmed","description":"The store confirmed the commit."},
    {"id":"arc-ob-delivered","name":"Notice delivered","description":"The notice queue delivers an event notice to a subscriber.","payload":[{"name":"seq","type":"number"}]},
    {"id":"arc-ob-acknowledged","name":"Notice acknowledged","description":"The subscriber acknowledges the notice."},
    {"id":"arc-ob-publish-now","name":"Publish now","description":"The runtime that committed publishes the events it committed."},
    {"id":"arc-ob-sweep-due","name":"Outbox job due","description":"The outbox job of a tenant comes due."},
    {"id":"arc-ob-published","name":"Events published","description":"The unpublished events of the tenant were handed to subscribers."},
    {"id":"arc-rl-deploy-started","name":"Rolling deployment started","description":"A newer version starts beside the older one."},
    {"id":"arc-rl-commit","name":"Commit requested","description":"A running version makes a commit."},
    {"id":"arc-rl-committed","name":"Commit written","description":"The commit was written in the format of the version that made it."},
    {"id":"arc-rl-deploy-finished","name":"Rolling deployment finished","description":"The older version has stopped."},
    {"id":"pl-presented","name":"Preview link presented","description":"A reader presents a preview link."},
    {"id":"pl-shown","name":"Draft shown from a preview link","description":"The draft was shown to the reader."},
    {"id":"pl-refused","name":"Preview link refused","description":"The link was not accepted."},
    {"id":"iw-received","name":"Inbound delivery received","description":"An inbound webhook delivery arrives with its event key.","payload":[{"name":"key","type":"string"}]},
    {"id":"iw-run-started","name":"Workflow run started","description":"A run was started from an inbound delivery."},
    {"id":"iw-ignored","name":"Repeated delivery ignored","description":"A repeated delivery started nothing."},
    {"id":"cv-proposed","name":"Change proposed","description":"The assistant proposes a change for a preview."},
    {"id":"cv-previewed","name":"Preview shown","description":"The preview of a proposed change is shown."},
    {"id":"cv-confirmed","name":"Preview confirmed","description":"The person confirms the preview."},
    {"id":"cv-cancel","name":"Preview cancelled","description":"The person cancels or replaces the preview."},
    {"id":"cv-cancelled","name":"Proposal cancelled","description":"The proposed change is withdrawn."},
    {"id":"cv-apply-requested","name":"Apply requested","description":"The assistant asks for the change to be applied."},
    {"id":"cv-applied","name":"Change applied","description":"The change was committed."},
    {"id":"cv-refused","name":"Apply refused","description":"The change was not applied."},
    {"id":"cv-permission-withdrawn","name":"Permission withdrawn","description":"The person loses a permission during a conversation."},
    {"id":"cv-operation-run","name":"Operation run","description":"The assistant runs an operation for the person."},
    {"id":"cv-operation-committed","name":"Operation committed","description":"The operation committed its change."},
    {"id":"cv-operation-refused","name":"Operation refused","description":"The operation was refused."},
    {"id":"saml-response","name":"SAML response presented","description":"A browser presents a SAML response with its assertion."},
    {"id":"saml-session-issued","name":"Session issued from a SAML assertion","description":"The assertion was accepted."},
    {"id":"saml-refused","name":"SAML response refused","description":"The assertion was not accepted."},
    {"id":"pw-attempt","name":"Password attempt","description":"A password is presented for an account.","payload":[{"name":"guess","type":"string"}]},
    {"id":"pw-accepted","name":"Password accepted","description":"The password was accepted."},
    {"id":"pw-refused","name":"Password refused","description":"The password attempt was refused."},
    {"id":"rt-published","name":"Event published","description":"The domain event was handed to subscribers."}
  ],
  "behaviors": [
    {"id":"emailed-link-flow","name":"Emailed link","subject":"identity-service","initial":"ml-idle","description":"One sign-in link: issued, presented, accepted once in the requesting browser within its lifetime of 15 ticks.","variables":[{"name":"issuedAt","type":"number","initial":0},{"name":"sessions","type":"number","initial":0}],"states":[{"id":"ml-idle","name":"No link"},{"id":"ml-pending","name":"Link issued"},{"id":"ml-used","name":"Link used"}],"transitions":[{"id":"ml-issue","from":"ml-idle","to":"ml-pending","on":"ml-requested","effects":[{"set":"issuedAt","to":"time"},{"emit":"ml-mailed"}]},{"id":"ml-accept-unchecked","from":"ml-pending","to":"ml-used","on":"ml-presented","faultOnly":true,"guard":"event.token == 'good'","description":"Defect: accepts the right token without checking lifetime or browser.","effects":[{"set":"sessions","to":"sessions + 1"},{"emit":"ml-session-issued"}]},{"id":"ml-accept","from":"ml-pending","to":"ml-used","on":"ml-presented","guard":"event.token == 'good' && event.browser == 'requester' && time - issuedAt <= 15","effects":[{"set":"sessions","to":"sessions + 1"},{"emit":"ml-session-issued"}]},{"id":"ml-refuse-pending","from":"ml-pending","to":"ml-pending","on":"ml-presented","effects":[{"emit":"ml-refused"}]},{"id":"ml-accept-again","from":"ml-used","to":"ml-used","on":"ml-presented","faultOnly":true,"description":"Defect: accepts a link that was already used.","effects":[{"set":"sessions","to":"sessions + 1"},{"emit":"ml-session-issued"}]},{"id":"ml-refuse-used","from":"ml-used","to":"ml-used","on":"ml-presented","effects":[{"emit":"ml-refused"}]}]},
    {"id":"oidc-callback-flow","name":"OpenID Connect callback","subject":"identity-service","initial":"oidc-idle","description":"One sign-in through a provider. The pending request carries the state value s1.","variables":[{"name":"federatedSessions","type":"number","initial":0}],"states":[{"id":"oidc-idle","name":"No request"},{"id":"oidc-awaiting","name":"Awaiting callback"},{"id":"oidc-done","name":"Signed in","terminal":true}],"transitions":[{"id":"oidc-begin","from":"oidc-idle","to":"oidc-awaiting","on":"oidc-started","effects":[{"emit":"oidc-redirected"}]},{"id":"oidc-accept-any-state","from":"oidc-awaiting","to":"oidc-done","on":"oidc-callback","faultOnly":true,"description":"Defect: accepts a callback without comparing its state value.","effects":[{"set":"federatedSessions","to":"federatedSessions + 1"},{"emit":"oidc-session-issued"}]},{"id":"oidc-accept","from":"oidc-awaiting","to":"oidc-done","on":"oidc-callback","guard":"event.state == 's1'","effects":[{"set":"federatedSessions","to":"federatedSessions + 1"},{"emit":"oidc-session-issued"}]},{"id":"oidc-refuse","from":"oidc-awaiting","to":"oidc-awaiting","on":"oidc-callback","effects":[{"emit":"oidc-refused"}]}]},
    {"id":"session-authority-flow","name":"Session authority","subject":"identity-service","initial":"sa-live","description":"The identity service's record of one session.","variables":[{"name":"revoked","type":"boolean","initial":false},{"name":"revokedAt","type":"number","initial":0}],"states":[{"id":"sa-live","name":"Live"},{"id":"sa-revoked","name":"Revoked"}],"transitions":[{"id":"sa-revoke","from":"sa-live","to":"sa-revoked","on":"sr-revoked","effects":[{"set":"revoked","to":true},{"set":"revokedAt","to":"time"},{"emit":"sr-notice"}]},{"id":"sa-answer-live","from":"sa-live","to":"sa-live","on":"sr-lookup","effects":[{"emit":"sr-lookup-answer","payload":{"valid":true}}]},{"id":"sa-answer-revoked","from":"sa-revoked","to":"sa-revoked","on":"sr-lookup","effects":[{"emit":"sr-lookup-answer","payload":{"valid":false}}]}]},
    {"id":"gateway-session-flow","name":"Gateway session copy","subject":"gateway","initial":"gs-ready","description":"The gateway's copy of the session. It trusts the copy for 5 ticks, then asks again.","variables":[{"name":"valid","type":"boolean","initial":true},{"name":"checkedAt","type":"number","initial":0},{"name":"staleAccept","type":"boolean","initial":false}],"states":[{"id":"gs-ready","name":"Ready"},{"id":"gs-checking","name":"Asking the identity service"}],"transitions":[{"id":"gs-hear-revocation","from":"gs-ready","to":"gs-ready","on":"sr-notice","effects":[{"set":"valid","to":false}]},{"id":"gs-accept-without-recheck","from":"gs-ready","to":"gs-ready","on":"sr-request","faultOnly":true,"guard":"valid","description":"Defect: trusts the copy however old it is.","effects":[{"set":"staleAccept","to":"staleAccept || (session-authority-flow.revoked && time - session-authority-flow.revokedAt >= 5)"},{"emit":"sr-accepted"}]},{"id":"gs-accept-fresh","from":"gs-ready","to":"gs-ready","on":"sr-request","guard":"valid && time - checkedAt < 5","effects":[{"set":"staleAccept","to":"staleAccept || (session-authority-flow.revoked && time - session-authority-flow.revokedAt >= 5)"},{"emit":"sr-accepted"}]},{"id":"gs-refuse-known","from":"gs-ready","to":"gs-ready","on":"sr-request","guard":"!valid","effects":[{"emit":"sr-refused"}]},{"id":"gs-recheck","from":"gs-ready","to":"gs-checking","on":"sr-request","guard":"valid && time - checkedAt >= 5","effects":[{"emit":"sr-lookup"}]},{"id":"gs-recheck-live","from":"gs-checking","to":"gs-ready","on":"sr-lookup-answer","guard":"event.valid == true","effects":[{"set":"checkedAt","to":"time"},{"set":"staleAccept","to":"staleAccept || (session-authority-flow.revoked && time - session-authority-flow.revokedAt >= 5)"},{"emit":"sr-accepted"}]},{"id":"gs-recheck-revoked","from":"gs-checking","to":"gs-ready","on":"sr-lookup-answer","guard":"event.valid == false","effects":[{"set":"valid","to":false},{"emit":"sr-refused"}]}]},
    {"id":"job-lease-flow","name":"Job lease","subject":"scheduler","initial":"jl-waiting","description":"One job. Every grant raises the token, and a result is recorded only with the current token.","variables":[{"name":"token","type":"number","initial":0},{"name":"completions","type":"number","initial":0},{"name":"acceptedToken","type":"number","initial":0}],"states":[{"id":"jl-waiting","name":"Waiting"},{"id":"jl-leased","name":"Leased"},{"id":"jl-done","name":"Completed"}],"transitions":[{"id":"jl-grant","from":"jl-waiting","to":"jl-leased","on":"job-due","effects":[{"set":"token","to":"token + 1"},{"emit":"lease-granted"}]},{"id":"jl-regrant","from":"jl-leased","to":"jl-leased","on":"lease-expired","effects":[{"set":"token","to":"token + 1"},{"emit":"lease-granted"}]},{"id":"jl-complete-any-token","from":"jl-leased","to":"jl-done","on":"work-reported","faultOnly":true,"description":"Defect: records a result without checking its token.","effects":[{"set":"completions","to":"completions + 1"},{"set":"acceptedToken","to":"event.token"},{"emit":"job-completed"}]},{"id":"jl-complete","from":"jl-leased","to":"jl-done","on":"work-reported","guard":"event.token == token","effects":[{"set":"completions","to":"completions + 1"},{"set":"acceptedToken","to":"event.token"},{"emit":"job-completed"}]},{"id":"jl-refuse-stale","from":"jl-leased","to":"jl-leased","on":"work-reported","effects":[{"emit":"result-refused"}]},{"id":"jl-refuse-after-done","from":"jl-done","to":"jl-done","on":"work-reported","effects":[{"emit":"result-refused"}]}]},
    {"id":"origin-content-flow","name":"Origin content","subject":"runtime","initial":"oc-live","description":"The published version of one page at the origin.","variables":[{"name":"version","type":"number","initial":1},{"name":"changedAt","type":"number","initial":0}],"states":[{"id":"oc-live","name":"Live"}],"transitions":[{"id":"oc-publish","from":"oc-live","to":"oc-live","on":"ec-published","effects":[{"set":"version","to":"version + 1"},{"set":"changedAt","to":"time"},{"emit":"ec-purge"}]},{"id":"oc-answer","from":"oc-live","to":"oc-live","on":"ec-origin-fetch","effects":[{"emit":"ec-origin-answer","payload":{"version":"version"}}]}]},
    {"id":"edge-copy-flow","name":"Edge copy","subject":"delivery-network","initial":"eg-ready","description":"The edge copy of the page. It is dropped by a purge and revalidated after a lifetime of 10 ticks.","variables":[{"name":"held","type":"number","initial":1},{"name":"storedAt","type":"number","initial":0},{"name":"staleServed","type":"boolean","initial":false}],"states":[{"id":"eg-ready","name":"Ready"},{"id":"eg-fetching","name":"Fetching from the origin"}],"transitions":[{"id":"eg-purge","from":"eg-ready","to":"eg-ready","on":"ec-purge","effects":[{"set":"held","to":0}]},{"id":"eg-serve-past-lifetime","from":"eg-ready","to":"eg-ready","on":"ec-request","faultOnly":true,"guard":"held > 0","description":"Defect: serves the copy however old it is.","effects":[{"set":"staleServed","to":"staleServed || (held != origin-content-flow.version && time - origin-content-flow.changedAt >= 10)"},{"emit":"ec-served"}]},{"id":"eg-serve","from":"eg-ready","to":"eg-ready","on":"ec-request","guard":"held > 0 && time - storedAt < 10","effects":[{"set":"staleServed","to":"staleServed || (held != origin-content-flow.version && time - origin-content-flow.changedAt >= 10)"},{"emit":"ec-served"}]},{"id":"eg-fetch","from":"eg-ready","to":"eg-fetching","on":"ec-request","effects":[{"emit":"ec-origin-fetch"}]},{"id":"eg-store","from":"eg-fetching","to":"eg-ready","on":"ec-origin-answer","effects":[{"set":"held","to":"event.version"},{"set":"storedAt","to":"time"},{"emit":"ec-served"}]}]},
    {"id":"provisioning-flow","name":"Tenant provisioning","subject":"control-plane","initial":"pv-idle","description":"Create the database, apply the layout, install the template, then report the tenant as active.","variables":[{"name":"database","type":"boolean","initial":false},{"name":"layout","type":"boolean","initial":false},{"name":"template","type":"boolean","initial":false},{"name":"active","type":"boolean","initial":false}],"states":[{"id":"pv-idle","name":"Idle"},{"id":"pv-creating","name":"Creating the database"},{"id":"pv-laying","name":"Applying the layout"},{"id":"pv-installing","name":"Installing the template"},{"id":"pv-active","name":"Active","terminal":true},{"id":"pv-failed","name":"Rolled back","terminal":true}],"transitions":[{"id":"pv-start","from":"pv-idle","to":"pv-creating","on":"pv-requested","effects":[{"emit":"pv-database-created"}]},{"id":"pv-activate-early","from":"pv-creating","to":"pv-active","on":"pv-database-created","faultOnly":true,"description":"Defect: reports the tenant active as soon as its database exists.","effects":[{"set":"database","to":true},{"set":"active","to":true},{"emit":"pv-activated"}]},{"id":"pv-created","from":"pv-creating","to":"pv-laying","on":"pv-database-created","effects":[{"set":"database","to":true},{"emit":"pv-layout-applied","after":2}]},{"id":"pv-laid","from":"pv-laying","to":"pv-installing","on":"pv-layout-applied","effects":[{"set":"layout","to":true},{"emit":"pv-template-installed","after":2}]},{"id":"pv-installed","from":"pv-installing","to":"pv-active","on":"pv-template-installed","effects":[{"set":"template","to":true},{"set":"active","to":true},{"emit":"pv-activated"}]},{"id":"pv-fail-laying","from":"pv-laying","to":"pv-failed","on":"pv-step-failed","effects":[{"set":"database","to":false},{"emit":"pv-rolled-back"}]},{"id":"pv-fail-installing","from":"pv-installing","to":"pv-failed","on":"pv-step-failed","effects":[{"set":"database","to":false},{"set":"layout","to":false},{"emit":"pv-rolled-back"}]}]},
    {"id":"proposal-flow","name":"Change proposal","subject":"agent-gateway","initial":"cp-idle","description":"A change is projected, then applied directly when policy classes it as safe, or after approval when it is risky.","variables":[{"name":"risky","type":"boolean","initial":false},{"name":"projected","type":"boolean","initial":false},{"name":"cleared","type":"boolean","initial":false},{"name":"applied","type":"boolean","initial":false}],"states":[{"id":"cp-idle","name":"No proposal"},{"id":"cp-projecting","name":"Projecting"},{"id":"cp-awaiting","name":"Awaiting approval"},{"id":"cp-ready","name":"Cleared"},{"id":"cp-closed","name":"Rejected"},{"id":"cp-done","name":"Applied","terminal":true}],"transitions":[{"id":"cp-open","from":"cp-idle","to":"cp-projecting","on":"cp-proposed","effects":[{"set":"risky","to":"event.risky"},{"emit":"cp-projected"}]},{"id":"cp-clear-safe","from":"cp-projecting","to":"cp-ready","on":"cp-projected","guard":"!risky","effects":[{"set":"projected","to":true},{"set":"cleared","to":true}]},{"id":"cp-hold-risky","from":"cp-projecting","to":"cp-awaiting","on":"cp-projected","guard":"risky","effects":[{"set":"projected","to":true}]},{"id":"cp-approve","from":"cp-awaiting","to":"cp-ready","on":"cp-approved","effects":[{"set":"cleared","to":true}]},{"id":"cp-reject","from":"cp-awaiting","to":"cp-closed","on":"cp-rejected"},{"id":"cp-apply-unapproved","from":"cp-awaiting","to":"cp-done","on":"cp-apply-requested","faultOnly":true,"description":"Defect: applies a risky change that nobody approved.","effects":[{"set":"applied","to":true},{"emit":"cp-applied"}]},{"id":"cp-refuse-awaiting","from":"cp-awaiting","to":"cp-awaiting","on":"cp-apply-requested","effects":[{"emit":"cp-refused"}]},{"id":"cp-apply-rejected","from":"cp-closed","to":"cp-done","on":"cp-apply-requested","faultOnly":true,"description":"Defect: applies a change that was rejected.","effects":[{"set":"applied","to":true},{"emit":"cp-applied"}]},{"id":"cp-refuse-closed","from":"cp-closed","to":"cp-closed","on":"cp-apply-requested","effects":[{"emit":"cp-refused"}]},{"id":"cp-apply","from":"cp-ready","to":"cp-done","on":"cp-apply-requested","effects":[{"set":"applied","to":true},{"emit":"cp-applied"}]}]},
    {"id":"arc-outbox-consumer-flow","name":"Notice subscriber","subject":"connector-runner","initial":"arc-oc-ready","description":"One subscriber receiving notices of one tenant. A notice whose sequence number is already applied is acknowledged and makes no further effect.","variables":[{"name":"applied","type":"number","initial":0},{"name":"effects","type":"number","initial":0}],"states":[{"id":"arc-oc-ready","name":"Ready"}],"transitions":[{"id":"arc-ob-apply","from":"arc-oc-ready","to":"arc-oc-ready","on":"arc-ob-delivered","guard":"event.seq > applied","effects":[{"set":"applied","to":"event.seq"},{"set":"effects","to":"effects + 1"},{"emit":"arc-ob-acknowledged"}]},{"id":"arc-ob-apply-again","from":"arc-oc-ready","to":"arc-oc-ready","on":"arc-ob-delivered","guard":"event.seq <= applied","faultOnly":true,"description":"Defect: makes the effect of a notice it has already applied.","effects":[{"set":"effects","to":"effects + 1"},{"emit":"arc-ob-acknowledged"}]},{"id":"arc-ob-skip-seen","from":"arc-oc-ready","to":"arc-oc-ready","on":"arc-ob-delivered","guard":"event.seq <= applied","effects":[{"emit":"arc-ob-acknowledged"}]}]},
    {"id":"arc-outbox-delivery-flow","name":"Outbox delivery after a stop","subject":"runtime","initial":"arc-od-idle","description":"A commit leaves events unpublished. The runtime that committed publishes them, or else the outbox job does.","variables":[{"name":"pending","type":"boolean","initial":false}],"states":[{"id":"arc-od-idle","name":"Nothing pending"},{"id":"arc-od-pending","name":"Events pending"},{"id":"arc-od-done","name":"Published","terminal":true}],"transitions":[{"id":"arc-od-commit","from":"arc-od-idle","to":"arc-od-pending","on":"rt-committed","effects":[{"set":"pending","to":true}]},{"id":"arc-od-publish-now","from":"arc-od-pending","to":"arc-od-done","on":"arc-ob-publish-now","effects":[{"set":"pending","to":false},{"emit":"arc-ob-published"}]},{"id":"arc-od-sweep","from":"arc-od-pending","to":"arc-od-done","on":"arc-ob-sweep-due","effects":[{"set":"pending","to":false},{"emit":"arc-ob-published"}]}]},
    {"id":"arc-rolling-change-flow","name":"Rolling change of format","subject":"runtime","initial":"arc-rc-old","description":"Two versions run together while a deployment replaces the older one. Commits are written in the older format until the older version has stopped.","variables":[{"name":"oldRunning","type":"boolean","initial":true},{"name":"newFormat","type":"boolean","initial":false}],"states":[{"id":"arc-rc-old","name":"Older version only"},{"id":"arc-rc-mixed","name":"Both versions running"},{"id":"arc-rc-new","name":"Newer version only"}],"transitions":[{"id":"arc-rl-start","from":"arc-rc-old","to":"arc-rc-mixed","on":"arc-rl-deploy-started"},{"id":"arc-rl-commit-early","from":"arc-rc-mixed","to":"arc-rc-mixed","on":"arc-rl-commit","faultOnly":true,"description":"Defect: writes the newer format while the older version still runs.","effects":[{"set":"newFormat","to":true},{"emit":"arc-rl-committed"}]},{"id":"arc-rl-commit-old","from":"arc-rc-mixed","to":"arc-rc-mixed","on":"arc-rl-commit","effects":[{"emit":"arc-rl-committed"}]},{"id":"arc-rl-finish","from":"arc-rc-mixed","to":"arc-rc-new","on":"arc-rl-deploy-finished","effects":[{"set":"oldRunning","to":false}]},{"id":"arc-rl-commit-new","from":"arc-rc-new","to":"arc-rc-new","on":"arc-rl-commit","effects":[{"set":"newFormat","to":true},{"emit":"arc-rl-committed"}]}]},
    {"id":"preview-link-flow","name":"Preview link","subject":"gateway","initial":"pl-issued","description":"One preview link, valid for 15 ticks from the time it is linked to the draft (issuedAt is 0 in the scenarios).","variables":[{"name":"issuedAt","type":"number","initial":0},{"name":"shown","type":"number","initial":0}],"states":[{"id":"pl-issued","name":"Issued"}],"transitions":[{"id":"pl-show-expired","from":"pl-issued","to":"pl-issued","on":"pl-presented","faultOnly":true,"description":"Defect: shows the draft after its expiry.","effects":[{"set":"shown","to":"shown + 1"},{"emit":"pl-shown"}]},{"id":"pl-show","from":"pl-issued","to":"pl-issued","on":"pl-presented","guard":"time - issuedAt < 15","effects":[{"set":"shown","to":"shown + 1"},{"emit":"pl-shown"}]},{"id":"pl-refuse","from":"pl-issued","to":"pl-issued","on":"pl-presented","effects":[{"emit":"pl-refused"}]}]},
    {"id":"inbound-run-flow","name":"Inbound delivery","subject":"workflow-engine","initial":"iw-idle","description":"One event key. The first delivery starts a run and a repeated delivery of the same event starts nothing.","variables":[{"name":"runs","type":"number","initial":0}],"states":[{"id":"iw-idle","name":"No delivery"},{"id":"iw-accepted","name":"Run started"}],"transitions":[{"id":"iw-first","from":"iw-idle","to":"iw-accepted","on":"iw-received","effects":[{"set":"runs","to":"runs + 1"},{"emit":"iw-run-started"}]},{"id":"iw-accept-again","from":"iw-accepted","to":"iw-accepted","on":"iw-received","faultOnly":true,"description":"Defect: starts a second run for a repeated delivery.","effects":[{"set":"runs","to":"runs + 1"},{"emit":"iw-run-started"}]},{"id":"iw-repeat","from":"iw-accepted","to":"iw-accepted","on":"iw-received","effects":[{"emit":"iw-ignored"}]}]},
    {"id":"cv-change-flow","name":"Confirmed change","subject":"conversation-service","initial":"cf-idle","description":"One change proposed by the assistant: previewed, then applied only after the person confirms it.","variables":[{"name":"previewed","type":"boolean","initial":false},{"name":"confirmed","type":"boolean","initial":false},{"name":"applied","type":"boolean","initial":false}],"states":[{"id":"cf-idle","name":"No change"},{"id":"cf-previewed","name":"Preview shown"},{"id":"cf-confirmed","name":"Confirmed"},{"id":"cf-applied","name":"Applied","terminal":true},{"id":"cf-cancelled","name":"Cancelled","terminal":true}],"transitions":[{"id":"cf-propose","from":"cf-idle","to":"cf-previewed","on":"cv-proposed","effects":[{"set":"previewed","to":true},{"emit":"cv-previewed"}]},{"id":"cf-confirm","from":"cf-previewed","to":"cf-confirmed","on":"cv-confirmed","effects":[{"set":"confirmed","to":true}]},{"id":"cf-apply","from":"cf-confirmed","to":"cf-applied","on":"cv-apply-requested","effects":[{"set":"applied","to":true},{"emit":"cv-applied"}]},{"id":"cf-apply-unconfirmed","from":"cf-previewed","to":"cf-applied","on":"cv-apply-requested","faultOnly":true,"description":"Defect: applies a previewed change that the person has not confirmed.","effects":[{"set":"applied","to":true},{"emit":"cv-applied"}]},{"id":"cf-refuse-unconfirmed","from":"cf-previewed","to":"cf-previewed","on":"cv-apply-requested","effects":[{"emit":"cv-refused"}]},{"id":"cf-cancel","from":"cf-previewed","to":"cf-cancelled","on":"cv-cancel","effects":[{"emit":"cv-cancelled"}]},{"id":"cf-refuse-cancelled","from":"cf-cancelled","to":"cf-cancelled","on":"cv-apply-requested","effects":[{"emit":"cv-refused"}]}]},
    {"id":"cv-authority-flow","name":"Operation under withdrawable permission","subject":"conversation-service","initial":"ca-waiting","description":"One operation the assistant runs for a person. It commits only while the permission the person holds at that moment allows it.","variables":[{"name":"permitted","type":"boolean","initial":true},{"name":"applied","type":"boolean","initial":false}],"states":[{"id":"ca-waiting","name":"Awaiting run"},{"id":"ca-done","name":"Committed","terminal":true}],"transitions":[{"id":"ca-withdraw","from":"ca-waiting","to":"ca-waiting","on":"cv-permission-withdrawn","effects":[{"set":"permitted","to":false}]},{"id":"ca-run","from":"ca-waiting","to":"ca-done","on":"cv-operation-run","guard":"permitted","effects":[{"set":"applied","to":true},{"emit":"cv-operation-committed"}]},{"id":"ca-run-stale","from":"ca-waiting","to":"ca-done","on":"cv-operation-run","faultOnly":true,"description":"Defect: runs the operation on the permission held when the preview was made.","effects":[{"set":"applied","to":true},{"emit":"cv-operation-committed"}]},{"id":"ca-refuse","from":"ca-waiting","to":"ca-waiting","on":"cv-operation-run","guard":"!permitted","effects":[{"emit":"cv-operation-refused"}]}]},
    {"id":"saml-assertion-flow","name":"SAML assertion use","subject":"identity-service","initial":"sa-fresh","description":"One SAML assertion. The first presentation yields a session, and a presentation after it is refused.","variables":[{"name":"sessions","type":"number","initial":0}],"states":[{"id":"sa-fresh","name":"Not presented"},{"id":"sa-spent","name":"Presented"}],"transitions":[{"id":"sam-accept-replay","from":"sa-spent","to":"sa-spent","on":"saml-response","faultOnly":true,"description":"Defect: accepts an assertion that was already used.","effects":[{"set":"sessions","to":"sessions + 1"},{"emit":"saml-session-issued"}]},{"id":"sam-accept","from":"sa-fresh","to":"sa-spent","on":"saml-response","effects":[{"set":"sessions","to":"sessions + 1"},{"emit":"saml-session-issued"}]},{"id":"sam-refuse","from":"sa-spent","to":"sa-spent","on":"saml-response","effects":[{"emit":"saml-refused"}]}]},
    {"id":"guess-throttle-flow","name":"Password guessing throttle","subject":"identity-service","initial":"gt-open","description":"Password attempts for one realm. Three failures close the throttle, and an attempt evaluated while it is closed is counted.","variables":[{"name":"failures","type":"number","initial":0},{"name":"throttled","type":"number","initial":0}],"states":[{"id":"gt-open","name":"Accepting attempts"}],"transitions":[{"id":"gt-ignore-throttle","from":"gt-open","to":"gt-open","on":"pw-attempt","faultOnly":true,"guard":"failures >= 3","description":"Defect: evaluates an attempt after the throttle has closed.","effects":[{"set":"throttled","to":"throttled + 1"},{"emit":"pw-refused"}]},{"id":"gt-refuse","from":"gt-open","to":"gt-open","on":"pw-attempt","guard":"failures >= 3","effects":[{"emit":"pw-refused"}]},{"id":"gt-wrong","from":"gt-open","to":"gt-open","on":"pw-attempt","guard":"failures < 3 && event.guess == 'wrong'","effects":[{"set":"failures","to":"failures + 1"},{"emit":"pw-refused"}]},{"id":"gt-right","from":"gt-open","to":"gt-open","on":"pw-attempt","guard":"failures < 3 && event.guess == 'right'","effects":[{"emit":"pw-accepted"}]}]},
    {"id":"commit-flow","name":"Commit and publication","subject":"runtime","initial":"rc-idle","description":"An accepted intent is committed, and only then is its event published.","variables":[{"name":"committed","type":"boolean","initial":false},{"name":"published","type":"boolean","initial":false}],"states":[{"id":"rc-idle","name":"Idle"},{"id":"rc-deciding","name":"Deciding"},{"id":"rc-committing","name":"Committing"},{"id":"rc-done","name":"Published","terminal":true}],"transitions":[{"id":"rc-decide","from":"rc-idle","to":"rc-deciding","on":"rt-intent","effects":[{"emit":"rt-decided"}]},{"id":"rc-publish-early","from":"rc-deciding","to":"rc-committing","on":"rt-decided","faultOnly":true,"description":"Defect: publishes the event before the commit is confirmed.","effects":[{"set":"published","to":true},{"emit":"rt-published"},{"emit":"rt-committed","after":1}]},{"id":"rc-commit","from":"rc-deciding","to":"rc-committing","on":"rt-decided","effects":[{"emit":"rt-committed","after":1}]},{"id":"rc-publish","from":"rc-committing","to":"rc-done","on":"rt-committed","effects":[{"set":"committed","to":true},{"set":"published","to":true},{"emit":"rt-published"}]}]}
  ],
  "faults": [
    {"id":"defect-link-replay","name":"A used link is accepted again","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"ml-accept-again","description":"The defect that IDN-003 forbids."},
    {"id":"defect-link-unchecked","name":"A link is accepted without lifetime or browser checks","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"ml-accept-unchecked","description":"The defect that IDN-004 and IDN-005 forbid."},
    {"id":"link-acceptance-disabled","name":"Links cannot be accepted","kind":"disable-transition","transition":"ml-accept","description":"Shows that the acceptance claim can fail."},
    {"id":"defect-oidc-state-unchecked","name":"A callback is accepted without comparing its state","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"oidc-accept-any-state","description":"The defect that FED-001 forbids."},
    {"id":"oidc-acceptance-disabled","name":"Callbacks cannot be accepted","kind":"disable-transition","transition":"oidc-accept","description":"Shows that the acceptance claim can fail."},
    {"id":"revocation-notice-dropped","name":"The revocation notice is dropped","kind":"drop-event","event":"sr-notice","description":"A gateway does not hear about a revocation.","realises":"fm-revocation-notice-lost"},
    {"id":"defect-gateway-no-recheck","name":"The gateway trusts its session copy forever","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"gs-accept-without-recheck","description":"The defect that IDN-013 forbids."},
    {"id":"defect-result-token-unchecked","name":"A result is recorded without checking its token","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"jl-complete-any-token","description":"The defect that SCH-011 forbids."},
    {"id":"completion-disabled","name":"Results cannot be recorded","kind":"disable-transition","transition":"jl-complete","description":"Shows that the completion claim can fail."},
    {"id":"purge-dropped","name":"The purge is dropped","kind":"drop-event","event":"ec-purge","description":"The content delivery network does not hear about a change.","realises":"fm-purge-lost"},
    {"id":"defect-edge-ignores-lifetime","name":"The edge serves a copy past its lifetime","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"eg-serve-past-lifetime","description":"The defect that EDG-006 forbids."},
    {"id":"defect-early-activation","name":"A tenant is reported active before it is ready","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"pv-activate-early","description":"The defect that TEN-002 forbids."},
    {"id":"defect-apply-unapproved","name":"A risky change is applied without approval","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"cp-apply-unapproved","description":"The defect that AGT-011 forbids."},
    {"id":"defect-apply-rejected","name":"A rejected change is applied","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"cp-apply-rejected","description":"The defect that AGT-011 forbids, on a rejected proposal."},
    {"id":"arc-defect-outbox-duplicate-applied","name":"A redelivered notice makes its effect again","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"arc-ob-apply-again","description":"The defect that ARC-104 forbids."},
    {"id":"arc-publisher-stops","name":"The runtime stops before it publishes","kind":"disable-transition","transition":"arc-od-publish-now","description":"A runtime crashes after its commit and before its publication."},
    {"id":"arc-recovery-disabled","name":"The outbox job does not publish","kind":"disable-transition","transition":"arc-od-sweep","description":"Shows that the recovery claim can fail."},
    {"id":"arc-defect-new-format-early","name":"A commit writes the newer format during a rolling deployment","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"arc-rl-commit-early","description":"The defect that ARC-106 forbids."},
    {"id":"defect-webhook-no-dedupe","name":"A repeated delivery starts a second run","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"iw-accept-again","description":"The defect that INT-151 forbids."},
    {"id":"defect-preview-unchecked","name":"A preview link shows the draft after its expiry","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"pl-show-expired","description":"The defect that CMS-159 forbids."},
    {"id":"defect-cv-apply-unconfirmed","name":"A preview is applied without confirmation","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"cf-apply-unconfirmed","description":"The defect that CNV-206 forbids."},
    {"id":"defect-cv-apply-stale","name":"An operation runs on a permission the person no longer holds","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"ca-run-stale","description":"The defect that CNV-203 forbids."},
    {"id":"cv-run-disabled","name":"Operations cannot be committed","kind":"disable-transition","transition":"ca-run","description":"Shows that the commit claim can fail."},
    {"id":"defect-saml-replay-accepted","name":"A used SAML assertion is accepted again","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"sam-accept-replay","description":"The defect that FED-006 forbids."},
    {"id":"defect-throttle-ignored","name":"A guess is evaluated after the throttle closes","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"gt-ignore-throttle","description":"The defect that IDN-250 forbids."},
    {"id":"defect-publish-before-commit","name":"An event is published before its commit","kind":"enable-transition","transition":"rc-publish-early","description":"The defect that RUN-005 forbids."}
  ],
  "scenarios": [
    {"id":"link-used-twice","name":"A link is used, then presented again","description":"The second presentation is refused.","behaviors":["emailed-link-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"ml-requested"},{"at":2,"event":"ml-presented","payload":{"token":"good","browser":"requester"},"note":"The person follows the link."},{"at":4,"event":"ml-presented","payload":{"token":"good","browser":"requester"},"note":"The same link again."}]},
    {"id":"link-presented-late","name":"A link is presented after its lifetime","description":"The lifetime is 15 ticks.","behaviors":["emailed-link-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"ml-requested"},{"at":30,"event":"ml-presented","payload":{"token":"good","browser":"requester"}}]},
    {"id":"link-presented-elsewhere","name":"A link is presented in another browser","description":"The link reached someone who did not ask for it.","behaviors":["emailed-link-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"ml-requested"},{"at":2,"event":"ml-presented","payload":{"token":"good","browser":"other"}}]},
    {"id":"oidc-sign-in","name":"Sign-in through a provider","description":"The callback carries the pending state.","behaviors":["oidc-callback-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"oidc-started"},{"at":3,"event":"oidc-callback","payload":{"state":"s1"}}]},
    {"id":"oidc-forged-callback","name":"A forged callback","description":"The callback carries a state that matches no pending request.","behaviors":["oidc-callback-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"oidc-started"},{"at":3,"event":"oidc-callback","payload":{"state":"forged"}}]},
    {"id":"revocation-heard","name":"A revocation reaches the gateway","description":"The next request is refused.","behaviors":["session-authority-flow","gateway-session-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"sr-request"},{"at":1,"event":"sr-revoked"},{"at":2,"event":"sr-request"}]},
    {"id":"revocation-notice-lost","name":"The revocation notice is lost","description":"A request inside the bound is still accepted. A request after it makes the gateway ask again, and is refused.","behaviors":["session-authority-flow","gateway-session-flow"],"faults":["revocation-notice-dropped"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"sr-request"},{"at":1,"event":"sr-revoked"},{"at":3,"event":"sr-request","note":"Within the bound of 5 ticks."},{"at":10,"event":"sr-request","note":"After the bound."}]},
    {"id":"lease-takeover","name":"A stalled worker is replaced","description":"The first worker stalls, the lease expires, a second worker gets the job, and then both report.","behaviors":["job-lease-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"job-due"},{"at":5,"event":"lease-expired"},{"at":6,"event":"work-reported","payload":{"token":1},"note":"The stalled worker wakes up."},{"at":7,"event":"work-reported","payload":{"token":2},"note":"The replacement finishes."}]},
    {"id":"page-purged","name":"A change purges the edge copy","description":"The next reader gets the new version.","behaviors":["origin-content-flow","edge-copy-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"ec-request"},{"at":1,"event":"ec-published"},{"at":2,"event":"ec-request"}]},
    {"id":"page-purge-lost","name":"The purge is lost","description":"A reader inside the lifetime still gets the old version. A reader after it gets the new one.","behaviors":["origin-content-flow","edge-copy-flow"],"faults":["purge-dropped"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"ec-request"},{"at":1,"event":"ec-published"},{"at":3,"event":"ec-request","note":"Within the lifetime of 10 ticks."},{"at":12,"event":"ec-request","note":"After the lifetime."}]},
    {"id":"tenant-provisioned","name":"A tenant is provisioned","description":"Every step succeeds.","behaviors":["provisioning-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"pv-requested"}]},
    {"id":"tenant-provisioning-fails","name":"Provisioning fails while applying the layout","description":"The layout step fails and what was created is removed.","behaviors":["provisioning-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"pv-requested"},{"at":1,"event":"pv-step-failed"}]},
    {"id":"safe-change-applied","name":"A safe change","description":"Policy classes the change as safe, so it is applied after its projection.","behaviors":["proposal-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"cp-proposed","payload":{"risky":false}},{"at":1,"event":"cp-apply-requested"}]},
    {"id":"risky-change-approved","name":"A risky change, approved","description":"An apply before approval is refused. After approval it goes through.","behaviors":["proposal-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"cp-proposed","payload":{"risky":true}},{"at":1,"event":"cp-apply-requested","note":"Too early."},{"at":2,"event":"cp-approved"},{"at":3,"event":"cp-apply-requested"}]},
    {"id":"risky-change-rejected","name":"A risky change, rejected","description":"The change is never applied.","behaviors":["proposal-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"cp-proposed","payload":{"risky":true}},{"at":1,"event":"cp-rejected"},{"at":2,"event":"cp-apply-requested"}]},
    {"id":"arc-outbox-duplicate-delivery","name":"A notice is delivered twice","description":"The notice queue delivers one event notice again before it is acknowledged.","behaviors":["arc-outbox-consumer-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"arc-ob-delivered","payload":{"seq":1}},{"at":2,"event":"arc-ob-delivered","payload":{"seq":1},"note":"The redelivery."}]},
    {"id":"arc-publisher-crashed-after-commit","name":"The publisher stops after a commit","description":"The runtime that committed stops before it publishes. The outbox job publishes later.","behaviors":["arc-outbox-delivery-flow"],"faults":["arc-publisher-stops"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"rt-committed"},{"at":1,"event":"arc-ob-publish-now"},{"at":5,"event":"arc-ob-sweep-due"}]},
    {"id":"arc-rolling-deploy-with-commit","name":"A commit during a rolling deployment","description":"The newer version starts and commits, the older version stops, and the newer version commits again.","behaviors":["arc-rolling-change-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"arc-rl-deploy-started"},{"at":1,"event":"arc-rl-commit"},{"at":3,"event":"arc-rl-deploy-finished"},{"at":4,"event":"arc-rl-commit"}]},
    {"id":"inbound-repeated-delivery","name":"An inbound delivery repeated","description":"The same event arrives twice, and the second arrival starts nothing.","behaviors":["inbound-run-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"iw-received","payload":{"key":"d1"}},{"at":2,"event":"iw-received","payload":{"key":"d1"},"note":"The sender retries."}]},
    {"id":"preview-presented-late","name":"A preview link presented after its expiry","description":"The link is presented 30 ticks after it was linked, past its 15-tick lifetime.","behaviors":["preview-link-flow"],"steps":[{"at":30,"event":"pl-presented"}]},
    {"id":"cv-confirmed-apply","name":"A change is confirmed, then applied","description":"The apply follows the confirmation.","behaviors":["cv-change-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"cv-proposed"},{"at":1,"event":"cv-confirmed"},{"at":2,"event":"cv-apply-requested"}]},
    {"id":"cv-unconfirmed-apply","name":"A change is applied before confirmation","description":"The apply is refused unless the change was confirmed.","behaviors":["cv-change-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"cv-proposed"},{"at":1,"event":"cv-apply-requested","note":"Applied before the person confirmed."}]},
    {"id":"cv-cancelled-preview","name":"A preview is cancelled, then applied","description":"A cancelled change is refused.","behaviors":["cv-change-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"cv-proposed"},{"at":1,"event":"cv-cancel"},{"at":2,"event":"cv-apply-requested"}]},
    {"id":"cv-withdrawn-before-run","name":"A permission is withdrawn before the operation runs","description":"The operation is refused after the permission is withdrawn.","behaviors":["cv-authority-flow"],"steps":[{"at":1,"event":"cv-permission-withdrawn"},{"at":2,"event":"cv-operation-run"}]},
    {"id":"cv-permitted-run","name":"An operation runs with its permission","description":"The operation commits.","behaviors":["cv-authority-flow"],"steps":[{"at":1,"event":"cv-operation-run"}]},
    {"id":"saml-replayed","name":"An assertion is presented twice","description":"The second presentation is refused.","behaviors":["saml-assertion-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"saml-response"},{"at":2,"event":"saml-response","note":"The same assertion again."}]},
    {"id":"distributed-guessing","name":"Guesses from many sources","description":"Wrong guesses arrive until the throttle closes, and then a right guess arrives.","behaviors":["guess-throttle-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"pw-attempt","payload":{"guess":"wrong"}},{"at":1,"event":"pw-attempt","payload":{"guess":"wrong"}},{"at":2,"event":"pw-attempt","payload":{"guess":"wrong"}},{"at":3,"event":"pw-attempt","payload":{"guess":"wrong"},"note":"The fourth guess, after the throttle has closed."},{"at":4,"event":"pw-attempt","payload":{"guess":"right"}}]},
    {"id":"intent-committed","name":"An intent is committed and published","description":"The event follows the commit.","behaviors":["commit-flow"],"steps":[{"at":0,"event":"rt-intent"}]}
  ],

  // ---- Fault model -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  "environments": [
    {"id":"env-local","name":"Local container stack","description":"Every component and its dependencies in containers on one machine (D-22).","guarantees":[{"aspect":"zone-count","value":1,"source":"d-22"},{"aspect":"clock-skew","value":0,"unit":"millisecond","source":"d-22"}]},
    {"id":"env-cloud","name":"Cloud profile, one region","description":"The first cloud profile (D-23): managed containers across three zones, managed PostgreSQL with a standby, a content delivery network.","guarantees":[{"aspect":"zone-count","value":3,"source":"d-23"},{"aspect":"region-count","value":1,"source":"d-23"},{"aspect":"clock-skew","value":500,"unit":"millisecond","source":"a-clock-skew"},{"aspect":"message-duplication","value":"wake notices and purge calls may be delivered more than once","source":"d-12"},{"aspect":"storage-durability","value":"a confirmed commit survives the loss of one database node","source":"a-database-commit"}]}
  ],
  "failureModes": [
    {"id":"fm-worker-stalls","name":"A worker stalls while holding a lease","kind":"stop","target":"scheduler","scope":"process","rate":{"value":1,"per":"day","source":"a-planning-rates"},"description":"A worker stops responding and later resumes with the lease it held."},
    {"id":"fm-revocation-notice-lost","name":"A revocation notice is lost","kind":"loss","target":"arc-identity-publishes-revocation","scope":"instance","rate":{"value":1,"per":"week","source":"a-planning-rates"},"description":"A gateway instance does not hear that a session was revoked."},
    {"id":"fm-purge-lost","name":"A purge is lost","kind":"loss","target":"runtime-calls-network","scope":"provider","rate":{"value":1,"per":"week","source":"a-planning-rates"},"description":"A purge call does not reach the content delivery network."},
    {"id":"fm-provisioning-step-fails","name":"A provisioning step fails","kind":"dependency-outage","target":"control-plane","scope":"instance","rate":{"value":1,"per":"month","source":"a-planning-rates"},"description":"Creating the database, applying the layout or installing the template fails."},
    {"id":"fm-provider-outage","name":"An identity provider is unreachable","kind":"dependency-outage","target":"external-identity-provider","scope":"provider","rate":{"value":2,"per":"year","source":"a-planning-rates"},"description":"A tenant's identity provider does not answer."},
    {"id":"fm-runtime-crash","name":"The runtime crashes between commit and publication","kind":"crash","target":"runtime","scope":"process","rate":{"value":1,"per":"month","source":"a-planning-rates"},"description":"A process stops after a transaction commits and before its events are published."},
    {"id":"fm-copy-store-outage","name":"The copy store is unreachable","kind":"dependency-outage","target":"copy-store","scope":"zone","rate":{"value":2,"per":"year","source":"a-planning-rates"},"description":"Stored view copies cannot be read or written."}
  ],
  "faultModels": [
    {"id":"fault-model-launch","name":"Launch fault model","environment":"env-cloud","description":"The failures the design is meant to survive in the first cloud profile. Failures outside it, such as the loss of a region, are answered by a restore (NG-4).","modes":["fm-worker-stalls","fm-revocation-notice-lost","fm-purge-lost","fm-provisioning-step-fails","fm-provider-outage","fm-runtime-crash","fm-copy-store-outage"],"bounds":[{"scope":"zone","maxConcurrent":1,"source":"d-23"}]}
  ],

  // ---- Data model: records and the copies made of them -------------------------------------------
  "records": [
    {"id":"rec-tenant","name":"Tenant","owner":"control-plane","key":["tenant-id"],"fields":[{"name":"tenant-id","type":"tenant-id"},{"name":"state","type":"tenant-state"},{"name":"plan","type":"plan-id"},{"name":"placement-id","type":"placement-id","refersTo":"rec-placement"}],"retention":"Until the tenant is deleted (TEN-011)."},
    {"id":"rec-placement","name":"Placement","owner":"control-plane","key":["placement-id"],"fields":[{"name":"placement-id","type":"placement-id"},{"name":"cluster","type":"cluster-id"},{"name":"region","type":"region-id"},{"name":"database","type":"database-id"}],"retention":"Until the tenant is deleted or moved."},
    {"id":"rec-domain-binding","name":"Domain binding","owner":"control-plane","key":["host"],"fields":[{"name":"host","type":"host"},{"name":"tenant-id","type":"tenant-id","refersTo":"rec-tenant"},{"name":"certificate-state","type":"certificate-state"}],"retention":"Until the binding is removed (EDG-008)."},
    {"id":"rec-wake-entry","name":"Wake entry","owner":"control-plane","key":["tenant-id"],"fields":[{"name":"tenant-id","type":"tenant-id","refersTo":"rec-tenant"},{"name":"due-at","type":"timestamp"}],"retention":"Replaced on every change of the tenant's next due time."},
    {"id":"rec-principal","name":"Principal","owner":"identity-service","key":["principal-id"],"fields":[{"name":"principal-id","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"subject"},{"name":"kind","type":"'person' | 'service' | 'agent'"},{"name":"state","type":"principal-state"},{"name":"display-name","type":"display-name","personal":"name"},{"name":"email","type":"email-address","personal":"contact"}],"retention":"Until the principal is deleted, with the tenant at the latest."},
    {"id":"rec-credential","name":"Credential","owner":"identity-service","key":["credential-id"],"fields":[{"name":"credential-id","type":"credential-id"},{"name":"principal-id","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"subject"},{"name":"kind","type":"'password' | 'passkey' | 'totp'"},{"name":"secret-hash","type":"hash","personal":"credential"}],"retention":"Until replaced or the principal is deleted."},
    {"id":"rec-identity-link","name":"Identity link","owner":"identity-service","key":["link-id"],"fields":[{"name":"link-id","type":"link-id"},{"name":"principal-id","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"subject"},{"name":"provider-id","type":"provider-id","refersTo":"rec-provider-config"},{"name":"external-subject","type":"external-subject","personal":"identifier"}],"retention":"Until unlinked or the principal is deleted."},
    {"id":"rec-provider-config","name":"Identity provider configuration","owner":"identity-service","key":["provider-id"],"fields":[{"name":"provider-id","type":"provider-id"},{"name":"protocol","type":"'oidc' | 'saml'"},{"name":"issuer","type":"url"},{"name":"email-domain","type":"domain"},{"name":"client-secret","type":"wrapped-secret"}],"retention":"Until the tenant removes the provider."},
    {"id":"rec-session","name":"Sign-in session","owner":"identity-service","key":["session-id"],"fields":[{"name":"session-id","type":"session-id"},{"name":"principal-id","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"subject"},{"name":"secret-hash","type":"hash","personal":"credential"},{"name":"authenticated-at","type":"timestamp"},{"name":"expires-at","type":"timestamp"},{"name":"revoked-at","type":"timestamp"}],"retention":"A day after it ends."},
    {"id":"rec-challenge","name":"Sign-in challenge","owner":"identity-service","key":["challenge-id"],"fields":[{"name":"challenge-id","type":"challenge-id"},{"name":"kind","type":"'link' | 'oidc' | 'saml'"},{"name":"token-hash","type":"hash","personal":"credential"},{"name":"email","type":"email-address","personal":"contact"},{"name":"browser-binding","type":"hash"},{"name":"expires-at","type":"timestamp"},{"name":"consumed","type":"boolean"}],"retention":"Until consumed or expired."},
    {"id":"rec-grant","name":"Grant","owner":"identity-service","key":["grant-id"],"fields":[{"name":"grant-id","type":"grant-id"},{"name":"principal-id","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"subject"},{"name":"delegator","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"party"},{"name":"scopes","type":"string[]"},{"name":"revoked-at","type":"timestamp"}],"retention":"Until revoked and the token lifetime has passed."},
    {"id":"rec-schema","name":"Tenant schema","owner":"runtime","key":["schema-version"],"fields":[{"name":"schema-version","type":"number"},{"name":"definition","type":"schema"}],"retention":"Every version is kept in the schema history."},
    {"id":"rec-content","name":"Content record","owner":"runtime","key":["object","record-id"],"fields":[{"name":"object","type":"object-type-id"},{"name":"record-id","type":"record-id"},{"name":"version","type":"number"},{"name":"status","type":"workflow-state"},{"name":"fields","type":"value-map"},{"name":"created-by","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"party"}],"retention":"Until deleted by the tenant, with every version (CMS-006)."},
    {"id":"rec-event","name":"Domain event","owner":"runtime","key":["seq"],"fields":[{"name":"seq","type":"number"},{"name":"revision","type":"number"},{"name":"body","type":"event-body"},{"name":"actor","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"party"},{"name":"correlation","type":"correlation-id"}],"retention":"For the life of the tenant."},
    {"id":"rec-job","name":"Job","owner":"scheduler","key":["job-id"],"fields":[{"name":"job-id","type":"job-id"},{"name":"due-at","type":"timestamp"},{"name":"state","type":"job-state"},{"name":"attempt","type":"number"},{"name":"lease-token","type":"number"},{"name":"idempotency-key","type":"string"}],"retention":"Thirty days after its outcome."},
    {"id":"rec-schedule","name":"Schedule","owner":"scheduler","key":["schedule-id"],"fields":[{"name":"schedule-id","type":"schedule-id"},{"name":"rule","type":"recurrence"},{"name":"paused","type":"boolean"},{"name":"next-due","type":"timestamp"}],"retention":"Until removed by the tenant."},
    {"id":"rec-workflow-run","name":"Workflow run","owner":"workflow-engine","key":["run-id"],"fields":[{"name":"run-id","type":"run-id"},{"name":"workflow","type":"workflow-id"},{"name":"state","type":"run-state"},{"name":"step","type":"number"}],"retention":"Ninety days after it ends."},
    {"id":"rec-audit-entry","name":"Audit entry","owner":"audit-log","key":["seq"],"fields":[{"name":"seq","type":"number"},{"name":"actor","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"party"},{"name":"on-behalf-of","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"party"},{"name":"action","type":"string"},{"name":"outcome","type":"string"},{"name":"correlation","type":"correlation-id"},{"name":"previous-hash","type":"hash"}],"retention":"For the life of the tenant, or the period its owner sets."},
    {"id":"rec-proposal","name":"Change proposal","owner":"agent-gateway","key":["proposal-id"],"fields":[{"name":"proposal-id","type":"proposal-id"},{"name":"author","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"party"},{"name":"approver","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"party"},{"name":"change","type":"change-set"},{"name":"projected-at-revision","type":"number"},{"name":"state","type":"proposal-state"}],"retention":"A year after it is closed."},
    {"id":"rec-submission","name":"Form submission","owner":"runtime","key":["submission-id"],"fields":[{"name":"submission-id","type":"submission-id"},{"name":"form","type":"form-id"},{"name":"submitted-at","type":"timestamp"},{"name":"email","type":"email-address","personal":"contact"},{"name":"values","type":"value-map","personal":"contact"}],"retention":"Until the retention period of its form ends (FRM-153)."},
    {"id":"rec-support-grant","name":"Support grant","owner":"identity-service","key":["grant-id"],"fields":[{"name":"grant-id","type":"grant-id"},{"name":"operator","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"party"},{"name":"issued-by","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"party"},{"name":"ends-at","type":"timestamp"},{"name":"withdrawn-at","type":"timestamp"}],"retention":"Until the grant ends. The audit entries that name it are kept with the tenant."},
    {"id":"rec-cnv-conversation","name":"Conversation","owner":"conversation-service","key":["conversation-id"],"fields":[{"name":"conversation-id","type":"conversation-id"},{"name":"principal-id","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"subject"},{"name":"started-at","type":"timestamp"},{"name":"state","type":"'open' | 'closed'"}],"retention":"Until the person or the tenant deletes it, and with the tenant at the latest (CNV-229)."},
    {"id":"rec-cnv-turn","name":"Turn","owner":"conversation-service","key":["turn-id"],"fields":[{"name":"turn-id","type":"turn-id"},{"name":"conversation-id","type":"conversation-id","refersTo":"rec-cnv-conversation"},{"name":"actor","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"party"},{"name":"body","type":"structured-blocks","personal":"activity"},{"name":"state","type":"'streaming' | 'complete' | 'interrupted' | 'failed'"},{"name":"correlation","type":"correlation-id"}],"retention":"Until its conversation is deleted (CNV-229)."},
    {"id":"rec-cnv-pending-action","name":"Pending action","owner":"conversation-service","key":["pending-id"],"fields":[{"name":"pending-id","type":"pending-id"},{"name":"conversation-id","type":"conversation-id","refersTo":"rec-cnv-conversation"},{"name":"person","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"party"},{"name":"assistant","type":"principal-id","refersTo":"principal","role":"party"},{"name":"change","type":"change-set"},{"name":"projected-at-revision","type":"number"},{"name":"state","type":"'previewed' | 'confirmed' | 'applied' | 'cancelled' | 'refused'"},{"name":"proposal-id","type":"proposal-id","refersTo":"rec-proposal"}],"retention":"Ninety days after it is closed."},
    {"id":"rec-file","name":"Stored file","owner":"file-store","key":["content-hash"],"fields":[{"name":"content-hash","type":"hash"},{"name":"size","type":"number"},{"name":"media-type","type":"string"}],"retention":"Until no record refers to it."}
  ],
  "copies": [
    {"id":"copy-compiled-schema","name":"Compiled schema","of":["rec-schema"],"heldBy":"runtime","scope":"internal","freshness":{"bound":"zero","mechanism":"keyed by tenant and schema version, so a new version is a new entry","source":"d-14"},"description":"copy-classes: compiled-schema."},
    {"id":"copy-directory-entry","name":"Directory entry","of":["rec-tenant","rec-placement","rec-domain-binding"],"fields":["rec-tenant.tenant-id","state","cluster","region","database","host"],"heldBy":"gateway","scope":"internal","freshness":{"bound":30,"unit":"second","mechanism":"refreshed from the tenant directory","source":"d-2"},"description":"copy-classes: directory-entry."},
    {"id":"copy-session-assertion","name":"Session assertion","of":["rec-session"],"fields":["session-id","rec-session.principal-id","authenticated-at","expires-at"],"heldBy":"gateway","scope":"per-session","freshness":{"bound":5,"unit":"second","mechanism":"revocation notice, and a recheck when the copy is older than the bound","source":"idn-014"},"erasure":{"point":"the revocation notice, or the next recheck","bound":5,"unit":"second","source":"idn-014"},"dependsOnAuthority":true,"description":"copy-classes: session-assertion."},
    {"id":"copy-public-view","name":"Public view","of":["rec-content"],"fields":["object","record-id","version","status","fields"],"heldBy":"copy-store","scope":"shared","freshness":{"bound":"zero","mechanism":"the key contains the revision of every object type the view depends on","source":"d-14"},"description":"copy-classes: public-view. Holds published fields only and no principal."},
    {"id":"copy-audience-view","name":"Audience view","of":["rec-content"],"heldBy":"copy-store","scope":"per-principal","freshness":{"bound":"zero","mechanism":"the key contains the audience class and the revision of every object type the view depends on","source":"d-15"},"erasure":{"point":"superseded by the commit of the deletion, removed by tag within the bound","bound":2,"unit":"second","source":"cpy-009"},"dependsOnAuthority":true,"description":"copy-classes: audience-view."},
    {"id":"copy-edge-page","name":"Edge page","of":["rec-content"],"fields":["object","record-id","version","status","fields"],"heldBy":"delivery-network","scope":"shared","freshness":{"bound":5,"unit":"second","mechanism":"surrogate-key purge sent by the commit, with the lifetime as backstop","source":"edg-007"},"description":"copy-classes: edge-page."},
    {"id":"copy-runtime-directory-entry","name":"Directory entry held by the runtime","of":["rec-tenant","rec-placement","rec-domain-binding"],"fields":["rec-tenant.tenant-id","state","cluster","region","database","host"],"heldBy":"runtime","scope":"internal","freshness":{"bound":30,"unit":"second","mechanism":"refreshed from the tenant directory","source":"d-2"},"description":"copy-classes: directory-entry. The runtime holds the placement it opens a tenant database with."},
    {"id":"copy-cnv-model-context","name":"Model request context","of":["rec-cnv-turn","rec-content"],"heldBy":"model-provider","scope":"per-principal","freshness":{"bound":"zero","mechanism":"built from the current records for each request and held by the provider only for that request","source":"cnv-233"},"erasure":{"point":"the end of the request, or the retention the tenant contract sets with the provider, whichever is earlier","source":"cnv-235"},"dependsOnAuthority":true,"description":"The content of one model request, as far as the tenant policy permits it for the person served."},
    {"id":"copy-edge-media","name":"Edge media","of":["rec-file"],"heldBy":"delivery-network","scope":"shared","freshness":{"bound":"zero","mechanism":"the address is derived from the content","source":"d-16"},"description":"copy-classes: edge-media."}
  ]
}
